# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI agent keys — TRS dashboard, 1 Oct 2026
#
# Three keys, one per agent, so the spend page can be reconciled against Google
# AI Studio per key, and so a leaked or rate-limited key takes down one agent
# rather than all of them.
#
# Make them at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — one key per agent, named
# after the agent. Paste the values below, then set the same three in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT, and not theoretical: a WRONG key does not fail loudly.
# Gemini answers an invalid key with HTTP 400 "API key not valid". The callers
# treat that as "no result" and fall back to a default — so the dashboard keeps
# working and quietly produces worse output. This happened today: .env.local
# ships GEMINI_API_KEY_DRAFT_EMAIL as the literal string "your_gemini_api_key",
# and with it the housekeeping sweep named every company after its own domain
# ("Fengchen", "Getsolar") instead of asking the model at all.
#
# So: paste real values, and after deploying open /analytics/ai-spend and check
# that each agent shows calls. An agent at zero calls after use means its key is
# wrong, not that it was idle.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Housekeeping — files mail to a company, names unknown domains, reads email
# signatures. Runs on gemini-3.5-flash-lite. Highest call volume, lowest cost:
# about $0.0002 per domain decided, because it decides once per DOMAIN and not
# once per email.
GEMINI_API_KEY_HOUSEKEEPING=

# Client relationships — reads a thread, the company record and the company's
# archive, then says what to do next and drafts the reply with its sources.
# Runs on gemini-3.8-flash. About $0.028 a call; the prompt carries ~25k tokens
# of company record, which is most of the cost.
GEMINI_API_KEY_CRM=

# Ask AI — answers from the live web and, when a client is named, from that
# client's own file. Runs on gemini-3.8-flash with Google Search grounding.
# About $0.0064 a question. Search itself is free for the first 5,000 grounded
# requests a month across all Gemini 3.x models, then $14 per 1,000 — TRS uses
# roughly 200 a month, so it stays free.
GEMINI_API_KEY_ASKAI=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already set in production; listed so nothing here is a surprise.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY_DRAFT_EMAIL      the existing drafter and classifiers
#   GEMINI_API_KEY_EMAIL_ANALYSIS   embeddings and inbound analysis
#   GEMINI_API_KEY_INBOUND          inbound mail processing
#   GEMINI_API_KEY_NEWS             outbound signal scanning
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY               Opus — still used by Nexus strategy, the
#                                   pricing-matrix extractors and /api/chat
#
# Until the three keys above are set, each agent falls back to the shared keys
# in that order, so nothing breaks before you fill them in. The spend page shows
# which agent spent what either way, because attribution is by feature, not by
# key.
#
# Model choice can be overridden without a redeploy, which is also the rollback
# if gemini-3.8-flash under-reasons on a hard question:
#
#   GEMINI_MODEL_LITE=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#   GEMINI_MODEL_FLASH=gemini-3.6-flash
#   GEMINI_MODEL_PRO=gemini-3.1-pro-preview
#   GEMINI_MODEL_DEEP=gemini-3.8-flash      # -> gemini-3.1-pro-preview to escalate
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
